ly confused in a README badge update. The swap nearly rode out into the published\nrecord. This tripwire closes that failure mode permanently.\n\n**DOI truth-table (canonical):**\n| DOI | Version |\n|-----|---------|\n| `10.5281/zenodo.20173912` | v13 |\n| `10.5281/zenodo.20173920` | v12 |\n| `10.5281/zenodo.20162352` | Ouroboros runtime v6.3.0 |\n| `10.5281/zenodo.19944926` | Concept DOI (Lutar Invariant family) |\n\n### What this workflow does (HUKLLA T11)\n\n1. **Runs on every push to `main` and every PR** — catches drift before merge.\n2. **Parses `README.md`** for all `zenodo.NNNN` or `10.5281/zenodo.NNNN` patterns.\n3. For each DOI:\n   - Verifies `doi.org` resolution returns HTTP 2xx (detects dead/mis-typed DOIs).\n   - Fetches `https://zenodo.org/api/records/NNNN` and checks `.metadata.title` exists.\n   - Extracts the version token from the title (e.g. `v13`, `v6.3.0`).\n   - Cross-checks the version the README claims for that DOI against the Zenodo record title.\n4. **Fails hard** (`exit 1`) on any mismatch with a `::error::` annotation visible in the PR check UI.\n\n### Failure message format\n\n```\nDOI-TITLE MISMATCH: zenodo.XXXX — README claims vY but Zenodo title says vZ\n```\n\n### References\n- HUKLLA doctrine: `docs/HUKLLA.md` (T11 section)\n- Postmortem: v12/v13 DOI swap — zenodo.20173912 vs zenodo.20173920\n- Author: Lutar, Stephen P. | ORCID: https://orcid.org/0009-0001-0110-4173","createdAt":"2026-05-15T03:47:06Z","deletions":0,"headRefName":"feat/huklla-t11-doi-title-gate","isDraft":true,"labels":[],"mergeable":"UNKNOWN","number":38,"reviewDecision":"REVIEW_REQUIRED","statusCheckRollup":[{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-05-15T03:49:45Z","conclusion":"FAILURE","detailsUrl":"https://github.com/szl-holdings/ouroboros-thesis/actions/runs/25899161522/job/76118669643","name":"doi-title-gate","startedAt":"2026-05-15T03:49:12Z","status":"COMPLETED","workflowName":"huklla-t11-doi-title-gate"},{"__typename":"CheckRun","completedAt":"2026-05-